<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine's Heraskevych hails EU pushback against Russian athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057a23ef66e36830f940ae739353a45f1e9a6b82106c46084c68cb0e91309071</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-heraskevych-hails-eu-pushback-against-russian-athletes/a-80074375--dc77282142e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-heraskevych-hails-eu-pushback-against-russian-athletes/a-80074375?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As European countries challenge Russia's sporting return, Ukrainian Olympian Vladyslav Heraskevych believes the IOC is facing a 'very big crisis.'</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>IOC paves way for Russia's return to Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ebdf4cb9740e06cf01f0ced5a421ec15202e2058ce064e13745c163aeaa78ff</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:11Z</updated><published>2026-07-07T17:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ioc-paves-way-for-russia-s-return-to-olympics/a-77868069--eaa3a93e8b12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ioc-paves-way-for-russia-s-return-to-olympics/a-77868069?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian athletes will be able to take part in qualifying events for the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games. It comes two months after the IOC lifted restrictions for Russia's ally Belarus.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4af5867e016c652ec522fc850a60f9374eac5174463573954c932ca19e349e1b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish rider Marc Marquez announces MotoGP retirement, days after clinching record 8th world title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:420543efb47cc8c9f0cda81838a9f7af95b8cbba2f08763c3b99aa3716d05305</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T18:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930--3f20c4c08f5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marc Marquez took fans and his team by surprise when announcing this weekend's race in Valencia will be his last. The 33-year-old won a record eight MotoGP titles, including his rookie and retirement seasons.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia: Police clash with Besiktas fans at Israel club game</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92a6edc87b3cbbfe6126206cfdc67a6d6121318dce0dbb3c1d26e1f40aca884e</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111--302857b88ba0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey's Besiktas accused Georgian police of using "disproportionate" force during the game with Israel's Hapoel Beer-Sheva, which saw Besiktas fans unfurl a banner supporting Palestine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA says a cyberattack against it targeted a 'limited set of personal and business information'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:146ee7d204ad98b787f09d9f94c1f5837f7eb3762b8f10ea6948a423c2b0ce3c</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660--002158da7f55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-says-a-cyberattack-against-it-targeted-a-limited-set-of-personal-and-business-information/a-80062660?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World football's governing body says the cyberattack targeted personal and business information. They struck at a sensitive time for the under-fire organization and its president, Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Freigang banned — Germany star to miss 2027 World Cup</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e52a1168409cadffca78f404e898c8ec0f8d12734984add772f1bdd82123da5</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930--642807df4daf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany forward Laura Freigang has been suspended until October 2027 after missing three doping tests, ruling her out of next year's Women's World Cup in Brazil. Freigang has denied any intention to evade controls.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Joshua Kimmich critcizes Bayern bosses over Musiala health comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b21f4164790d86669a9042a7664f88e8cf5b1c2f24d9ec0d5e23007e94693287</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155--f8755c2422c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Kimmich has slammed Bayern Munich's leadership over comments about Jamal Musiala's health issues. The bosses have questioned whether the player can return to previous form – and is still worth his high salary.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey prospect Max Calce follows Leon Draisaitl's path, leaving Mannheim for Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddd4b4f484a353474d89a06169b75cef8bf90364990627789fd1daf91d9c6a9f</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458--4ca1ab8cf6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The player widely seen as Germany's biggest ice hockey talent to come along in years is leaving the country's top professional league for Canada – changing tracks in his bid to make it to the NHL.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women's football team take stand against domestic violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:749dbd4da2b6cd4e0feec987e03396a6336fa384ee67d0827e06b9b07d3e2095</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974--84aba926a54f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's women's football team are to wear UN Women badges in games against Argentina and Peru, as domestic violence hits a record high in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>CAS reinstates Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c3d506aea384b093c8ee77e88ea1b8035128f459e2b8f52e18d78867e229449</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027--561a21777065.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cas-reinstates-senegal-as-2025-afcon-champions/a-80021027?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has reinstated Senegal as 2025 AFCON champions, overturning a CAF decision that stripped them of the title. Morocco, previously declared winners, are confirmed runners-up.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e37a273253336cf4acbf92f2d3e36c58ffae6f0137e5742df57910fdc88ed7b2</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364dfff25dea55708f3fa0830298743c96547237aabba3c89aa39c2f66c2416b</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
